# guides

2 documents on this shelf, in the reading order this corpus derives.

- [GD-FIX-first-run](first-run.md) — what to do on a first run, and what to read when it refuses
- [GD-FIX-recovery](recovery.md) — how to recover a corpus whose lock and sources disagree (asserted, and no human has accepted it)

--- write into an empty tree ---
projections
  shelf_index generate/decisions/README.md
    written
  shelf_index generate/guides/README.md
    written

what this verb does not write, and why
  shelf_index generate/archive/README.md
    the shelf `archive` holds no document, and an index of nothing asserts that a shelf is there
  graph_export generate/export.json
    the emitters, the loss set and the projection census are issue #65, and an export that declared no loss set would be the untrusted projector spec 6 built the census to catch
  coverage_report the register
    its content is a function of the clock as well as of the corpus and the lock, because a migration task lapses and a suppression expires on a date. A committed copy would fail this check on a morning when nothing changed. Spec 13 carries it
  corpus_descriptor .headwater/corpus.json
    nothing computes a descriptor yet. Issue #64 owns it, and it writes through this verb when it lands
fails the run: false

